}
```

## 4. Implementation Steps
1. Initialize Vite Vue TypeScript project in `frontend/`:
   ```bash
   npm create vite@latest frontend -- --template vue-ts
   ```
2. Install core dependencies:
   ```bash
   cd frontend
   npm install vue-router@4 pinia@2 axios lucide-vue-next
   npm install -D tailwindcss postcss autoprefixer @types/node
   npx tailwindcss init -p
   ```
3. Configure `tsconfig.json` with strict type checking and `@/*` path alias mapping to `./src/*`.
4. Configure Vue Router with view routes: `/` (Dashboard), `/habits`, `/okrs`, `/journal`, `/login`.
5. Set up global dark mode provider in `App.vue`.

## 5. Security, Error Handling & Edge Cases
- **XSS Prevention:** Vue automatically escapes interpolated strings (`{{ }}`); never use `v-html` on unvetted inputs.
- **Routing Guards:** Protect authenticated routes (`/`, `/journal`, `/habits`) using Vue Router navigation guards, redirecting unauthenticated users to `/login`.

## 6. Verification & Automated Tests
- Run dev server:
  ```bash
  npm run dev
  ```
- Run type check & production build:
  ```bash
  npm run build
  ```
- Both commands must succeed with exit code `0`.

## 7. Definition of Done (DoD)
- [ ] Vue 3 SPA builds cleanly with Vite and TypeScript.
- [ ] TailwindCSS configured with dark mode and typography palette.
- [ ] Router routes configured with navigation guard stubs.
